        312.00425000000007,
        9.4724249999999302
      ],
      "text" : "said President Bush began the meeting with the words, “We’re at war,”5 and"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.660399999999981,
        504.10464999999994,
        312.01922500000001,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "that Director of Central Intelligence George Tenet said the agency was still"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.660399999999981,
        492.85424999999992,
        312.00874999999996,
        9.4728250000000571
      ],
      "text" : "assessing who was responsible, but the early signs all pointed to al Qaeda.6 That"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.660174999999981,
        481.60464999999999,
        312.01102500000002,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "evening the Deputies Committee returned to the pending presidential direc-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.66119999999998,
        470.35424999999998,
        191.77325000000002,
        9.4728250000000003
      ],
      "text" : "tive they had labored over during the summer.7"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        51.660000000000004,
        459.10505000000001,
        300.02980000000008,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "The secretary of defense directed the nation’s armed forces to Defense Con-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.661349999999999,
        447.85464999999999,
        311.99657500000001,
        9.472424999999987
      ],
      "text" : "dition 3, an increased state of military readiness.8 For the first time in history,"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.661250000000024,
        436.60464999999999,
        312.03972500000009,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "all nonemergency civilian aircraft in the United States were grounded, strand-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.661250000000024,
        425.35424999999998,
        312.05612499999995,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "ing tens of thousands of passengers across the country. Contingency plans for"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.662275000000022,
        414.10384999999997,
        312.03562499999998,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "the continuity of government and the evacuation of leaders had been imple-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.662275000000022,
        402.85344999999995,
        312.06420000000003,
        9.4736250000000268
      ],
      "text" : "mented.9 The Pentagon had been struck; the White House or the Capitol had"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.661124999999998,
        391.60464999999999,
        312.03665000000001,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "narrowly escaped direct attack. Extraordinary security precautions were put in"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.663174999999995,
        380.35424999999998,
        155.34694999999999,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "place at the nation’s borders and ports."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        51.659774999999996,
        369.10384999999997,
        300.02672500000006,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "In the late afternoon, the President overruled his aides’ continuing reluc-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.661124999999998,
        357.85344999999995,
        312.02742499999988,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "tance to have him return to Washington and ordered Air Force One back to"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.661124999999998,
        346.60304999999994,
        312.02639999999985,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "Andrews Air Force Base. He was flown by helicopter back to the White House,"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.663174999999995,
        335.35264999999993,
        311.97720000000004,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "passing over the still-smoldering Pentagon. At 8:30 that evening, President Bush"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.663174999999995,
        324.10224999999991,
        312.01307499999996,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "addressed the nation from the White House. After emphasizing that the first"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.663174999999995,
        312.8518499999999,
        312.03972499999998,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "priority was to help the injured and protect against any further attacks, he said:"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.663174999999995,
        301.60144999999989,
        312.08072499999992,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "“We will make no distinction between the terrorists who committed these acts"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.663174999999995,
        290.35104999999987,
        312.04792500000008,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "and those who harbor them.” He quoted Psalm 23—“though I walk through"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.663174999999995,
        279.10064999999986,
        312.02947500000005,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "the valley of the shadow of death . . .” No American, he said, “will ever forget"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.664199999999994,
        267.85024999999985,
        42.708165000000008,
        9.4768250000001331
      ],
      "text" : "this day.”10"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        51.660000000000004,
        256.60505000000001,
        299.99289999999985,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "Following his speech, President Bush met again with his National Security"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.660325,
        245.35465000000002,
        311.986425,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "Council (NSC), expanded to include Secretary of Transportation Norman"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.660325,
        234.10425000000001,
        311.98027499999995,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "Mineta and Joseph Allbaugh, the director of the Federal Emergency Manage-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.660325,
        222.85384999999999,
        311.98745000000002,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "ment Agency. Secretary of State Colin Powell, who had returned from Peru after"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.660325,
        211.60344999999998,
        309.1932000000001,
        9.4736250000000268
      ],
      "text" : "hearing of the attacks, joined the discussion. They reviewed the day’s events.11"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 12,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.660000000000004,
        175.19730000000001,
        222.59759999999997,
        10.871999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "10.1 IMMEDIATE RESPONSES AT HOME"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.660000000000004,
        152.35505000000001,
        311.98540000000008,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "As the urgent domestic issues accumulated, White House Deputy Chief of Staff"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.660000000000004,
        141.10464999999999,
        312.00690000000003,
        9.4724250000000154
      ],
      "text" : "Joshua Bolten chaired a temporary “domestic consequences” group.12 The"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.659974999999974,
        129.85464999999999,
        311.98642500000005,
        9.2864999999999895
      ],
      "text" : "agenda in those first days is worth noting, partly as a checklist for future crisis"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.659974999999974,
        118.60424999999999,
        311.84087499999981,
        9.2865000000000038
      ],
      "text" : "planners. It began with problems of how to help victims and stanch the flow-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        39.659974999999974,
        107.35384999999999,
        177.74319999999997,
        9.2865000000000038
      ],
      "text" : "ing losses to the American economy, such as"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        51.659649999999971,
        84.854074999999995,
        287.98604999999998,
        9.2865000000000038
      ],
      "text" : "• Organizing federal emergency assistance. One question was what kind"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        63.659324999999967,
        73.603674999999996,
        275.98739999999998,
        9.2865000000000038
      ],
      "text" : "of public health advice to give about the air quality in Lower Manhat-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10.25,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        63.659324999999967,
        62.353274999999996,
        168.01304250000004,
        9.4738000000000113
      ],
      "text" : "tan in the vicinity of the fallen buildings.13"
    }
